cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SpecRoute in academic work, blog posts, or other published material, please cite it as below."
title: "SpecRoute: An open-source framework for spec-driven agentic software engineering"
abstract: >-
  SpecRoute is a vendor-neutral framework for spec-driven agentic software
  engineering. It captures production-grade patterns for PRDs, specifications
  (requirements / design / tasks triplet), agents, skills, slash commands,
  hooks, prompts, workflows, and engineering rules across six agent CLIs:
  Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Kiro, Cursor, and Windsurf. The framework
  ships markdown content (templates, runtime layouts, worked examples)
  rather than application code; consumers drop the per-vendor runtime
  layouts into their own repositories and adapt the templates to their stack.
type: software
